>Actually - does anyone know the difference between the nh312pc and the
>nh312386 versions?  (the 286 version and the 386 version)
>...in other words, is it worth the effort to switch if I'm changing 
>computers?

The 386 version runs in DPMI, which allows the program to directly use
all available memory if you have a 386 or 486. It will also use the
disk as virtual memory allowing you to have up to 2 Gig of usable
memory (provided you have enough memory and hard disk space.  :-)

The normal version (nh312pc) runs with overlays to allow the program
to 'fit' in the 640k conventional memory segment.  Because it is
continually swapping from disk, it is much slower than the 386 version.

If you have a 386+ you should be using the 386 version.  If you don't
consider upgrading.

